# Secrets and sensitive data

- Never commit, push, sync, or paste into chat: API keys, PATs, passwords, shared secrets, private keys, or tokens.
- Never run commands that print credentials (e.g. `git credential fill`) into the terminal log.
- If a document that must go to git would contain secrets, replace values with `********` and add a note: "ver en archivos locales" (e.g. `.env` or password manager). Keep real values only in local gitignored files (`.env`) or a password manager.
- `.env` stays local; only `.env.example` (empty placeholders) may be committed.
- For GitHub auth on this project, use a dedicated token for this app — do not reuse or display tokens from other apps.
